{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Plugin Architecture","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.send()"},{"text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The generic ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A fifth method, ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","level":2,"anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Core Middleware","level":3,"anchor":"Core-Middleware"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"action-agnostic infrastructure"}]},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State: Equatable"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Domain Plugins","level":3,"anchor":"Domain-Plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain-specific modules"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Importing at call sites","level":3,"anchor":"Importing-at-call-sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because each domain plugin ships as a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"separate library target"}]},{"type":"text","text":", its state and action types are defined in that module — not in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":". A common convention is to re-export core Swidux from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":", but that re-exports "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"core Swidux only"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; it does not re-export the plugin modules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So any file that reads a plugin-owned slice ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.killswitch.*"},{"type":"text","text":", …) or dispatches a plugin action ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"type":"text","text":", …) must import that plugin’s module in "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"that"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallAction"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxPaywall"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"touches only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ui(...)"},{"text":" (app-module types) → nothing extra","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The easy case to forget is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}]},{"type":"text","text":" that reads the slice for display — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" already import the module, but the View is a different file. Without the import you get:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["property 'isOptedOut' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxAnalytics'","property 'isPro' is not available due to missing import of defining module 'SwiduxPaywall'"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is to add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Swidux<Plugin>"},{"type":"text","text":" to that file."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Comparison","level":3,"anchor":"Comparison"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}]}]]]},{"type":"heading","text":"The Decision Rule","level":2,"anchor":"The-Decision-Rule"},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Hook Selection Guide","level":2,"anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"flush() async","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Registration Order","level":2,"anchor":"Registration-Order"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost"},{"type":"text","text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","level":2,"anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verdictReceived"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshSucceeded"},{"type":"text","text":" — fires on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"type":"text","text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Do "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — or a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derived from it — instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"snapshot, then writes back via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply"},{"type":"text","text":". For a leaf slice that write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a plain assignment whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" setter equality-gates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-diffing consumer such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties"},{"type":"text","text":" (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", not of any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observers without any extra reducer logic."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Next Steps","level":2,"anchor":"Next-Steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference"},{"text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"reference"},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swidux","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"role":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"title":"Store","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"title":"Design Principles","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"title":"EntityStore","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"title":"UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"title":"PluginHost","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PluginHost"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"title":"Persistence Middleware","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"title":"Architecture & Performance","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article"}}}